-- title:
--   Straight-line segments of the BSP construction block: carve and leaf
-- statement:
--   Thirteen straight-line facts about the program $\mathrm{bd}$ of definition `DetANN_HPIMBuildProg`: the carve loop and the leaf node. Here the current box is at pointer 54, the current slot in pointer 55, the core box at pointer 48 and the axis in pointer 53.
--
--   Every conjunct has the same shape. Let $Q$ contain $\mathrm{bd}(o)$ at offset $o$ (`Embeds Q (bd off) off`), and let $s$ be a non-halted state at the stated pc with $1\le$ pointer 1 and the stated hypotheses. Then after exactly the stated number $t$ of steps, the run of $Q$ from $s$:
--   - is at the stated pc (relative to $o$) and has not halted;
--   - has the stated values in the changed registers and cells;
--   - leaves all other pointer and real registers and all other real and integer cells unchanged;
--   - has work $s.\mathrm{work}+t$, and its `cellsWritten` set consists of the listed cells.
--
--   Pointer 1 holds $m$, pointer 11 holds $n$, and $Z$, $R$ denote pointers 13, 14 of $s$.
--
--   1. **Carve start** $280\to283$ (3): pointers $54:=p_{43}$, $55:=p_{44}$, $53:=0$.
--   2. **Carve end** $283\to372$ (1): when $k\ge m$.
--   3. **No low peel** $283\to326$ (7): when $tlo_k-lo_k\le0$ (reals 44, 45).
--   4. **Low peel** $283\to258$ (21): when $tlo_k-lo_k>0$: a cut node $[1,p_{54}]$ at $Z-4$ with $I[p_{55}]:=Z-4$; copy-and-set of the current box with index $m+k$, value $tlo_k$ and code 2.
--   5. **Push the low slab** $304\to258$ (17): pushes $[\text{new box},\text{node}+2,\text{link}]$; copy-and-set of the current box with index $k$ and code 3.
--   6. **Continue** $321\to326$ (5): current box := the new box, current slot := node $+3$.
--   7. **No high peel** $326\to370$ (8): when $hi_k-thi_k\le0$.
--   8. **High peel** $326\to258$ (22): a cut node as in 4; copy-and-set with index $k$, value $thi_k$ and code 4.
--   9. **Push the high slab** $348\to258$ (18): pushes $[\text{new box},\text{node}+3,\text{link}]$; copy-and-set with index $m+k$ and code 5.
--   10. **Continue** $366\to283$ (6): current box := the new box, current slot := node $+2$, $k:=k+1$.
--   11. **Next axis** $370\to283$ (2): $k:=k+1$.
--   12. **Push the core** $372\to34$ (11): pushes $[p_{54},p_{55},\text{link}]$.
--   13. **Leaf** $383\to34$ (12): writes the leaf node $[0,p_{43},p_{61}]$ at $Z-3$ and $I[p_{44}]:=Z-3$.
-- source:
--   Original, written for the mission 'Deterministic Approximate Nearest Neighbors in High Dimensions' as part of a floor-free proof of DetANN.lemma_3_3 (Feng, Indyk, STOC 2027 submission, Lemma 3.3, p.7). These are pieces of the BSP construction block of DetANN.HPIM.build_block, split out so that each proof fits the verifier's time limit. The machine is PNormReg (definition PNormReg_Machine) with the conventions of DetANN_DataStructure.

